00:03:28.127 --> 00:03:29.547
"Is it true that stress can

00:03:29.547 --> 00:03:31.790
"lead to the growing of white hairs?"

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.400
Ursella Ariella, I gotta tell
you, I got them white hairs.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:40.210
What's happening is actually
you have a decrease in melanin

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:43.540
producing cells called
melanocytes in the hair follicle.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.980
If your hair's white, that means

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.250
you completely have lost all your melanin.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.580
But if you have some, you get gray hair,

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.260
so it's almost like partial
pigmentation, if you will.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.640
Now, the question you asked
is if stress effects it.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.880
We know genetics is the
most important thing,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.520
but stress seems to play a role in this.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.840
I've looked into this myself.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.440
We don't have a cause
and effect relationship.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.710
Let me tell you that out right,

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.300
but when we look into it, we
do see some sort of pattern

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.250
and correlation emerge between
those who don't sleep enough,

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.270
who have very competitive jobs,

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.420
high stress levels at
work, family members.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.520
They generally gray earlier.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.560
Our reasoning for this, which is unproven,

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.960
but what we think happens is
that there is an inflammatory

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.800
response from free radicals
that occurs from stress

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.280
and that actually interferes
with melanin process.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.830
Like the way that the color
is brought to the follicle.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.230
And when that happens, you're
more likely to gray earlier.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.440
While science hasn't given
us a definitive answer,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.150
I'm gonna give it a preliminary true

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:44.687
that stress does cause your
hair to turn gray sooner.

00:04:44.687 --> 00:04:47.177
"Is cracking my knuckles a bad idea?

00:04:47.177 --> 00:04:48.890
"Will I get arthritis?"

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.150
Well Henry, I can't promise

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.130
if you're gonna get arthritis or not.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.210
But what I can tell you
is that medical research

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.600
has looked into the science
of cracking knuckles

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.830
and that sound that you hear is actually

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:04.200
just nitrogen bubbles popping
in your synovial fluid.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.320
Synovial fluid is the stuff
that lubricates your joints

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.580
and when you hear that cracking,

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.310
you think that's a bad thing,
that it's your bones breaking

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.160
or anything like that.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.340
That's not really the case.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.270
It's these completely
harmless nitrogen bubbles

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:20.350
and there's been really
decent evidence that shows

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:22.320
it does not lead to arthritis

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.350
and unless it's causing you
some kind of pain or discomfort,

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:28.070
it's usually and
generally pretty harmless.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:30.300
If it makes you feel better,
psychologically speaking,

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.133
crack away.

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.510
And as long as you're not
bothering anybody, that's fine.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.070
Now, if you're getting
pain when you're cracking,

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.360
maybe you already have arthritis,

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.600
maybe you have a tendon injury.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.340
Definitely don't crack in those scenarios.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:43.300
If you find yourself
needing to crack otherwise

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.550
you do have pain, that
could also be a sign

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.390
that something's going on

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.940
and you should talk to your doctor,

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.770
but in general know that when
you crack your knuckles once

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:53.380
see like now, I can't crack them again.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.060
The reason why is because
you need to give time

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:58.880
for those nitrogen bubbles to
reform in the synovial fluid.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.260
It's kind of a fun fact for you.

